            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this recipe. I changed it a little. I sauteed onions first and then added the soup, tuna, eggs and I also added green peas. I just added the soup from the can and then added a little milk as needed adn it wasn't too soupy."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KimberlyKay"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I liked this recipe but tweaked it a bit hence only the 4 stars and not 5. I added about 1 tsp. pepper and 1/2 tsp. creole seasoning for more flavor and 1/3 cup flour to thicken it. I wouldn't suggest preparing the cream of mushroom soup according to label because that is how mine got so thin.",
            "datePublished": "2006-02-04T19:36:32.750Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BraveChop2797"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We had a family recipe like this, but you use 2 cans of drained tuna, then add 2 tsp. yellow mustard and (about) 3 Tblsp. Worcestershire sauce. The hard boiled eggs were chopped. We always served it on soda crackers. Salt &amp; pepper to taste. Not too appetizing to look at, but it’s delish!",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-07T01:29:52.852Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Moppel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "That was surprisingly tasty! I just added a little bit of pepper and a splash of evaporated milk. I did not add any other liquids, and it was perfect. The tuna flavor is not overpowering, and the eggs give it a nice touch. \nThank you for sharing this recipe, I would have never thought of combining those things!\nI will definitely make this again, it's quick and inexpensive. My super picky 8 year old is gobbling up the last bit of it right now.",
            "datePublished": "2017-01-30T15:45:18.600Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jayne Teske"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This has been a family recipe for 40 years. I do many of the variations that other reviews have suggested, but my one secret ingredient is a dash of Worcestershire sauce. Just a super easy meal when you are out of time.",
            "datePublished": "2015-01-30T17:40:11.747Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mjhoppers"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The reason you found it runny was because you are not supposed to add milk. Just put the can of mushroom soup into the pot and add the tuna. Then heat it up real hot and pour it over 2 buttered pieces of toast. One of my quickest favorite meals of all time.",
            "datePublished": "2012-07-19T13:45:10.633Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SJJ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Pretty good! Perfect for a chilly night/day. Easy. I took advice from the other reviews and only added 1/2 the milk and added lots of pepper. After it was dished up, I dashed a little Texas Pete on mine. I does lack a little spice. but other than that it was a hit!",
            "datePublished": "2010-12-14T16:27:06.423Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kaceygee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added a small can of mushrooms. Next time I will add milk instead of water and not much of it. I considered doubling the tuna.",
            "datePublished": "2017-01-17T01:02:04.097Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
